<p>I picked up a new &ldquo;Mozzarella cheese&rdquo; from a vegan brand I like. I understand the marketing, but calling vegan products cheese or meat is bullshit. They don’t taste like the real thing. People who look to replace the real thing with the &ldquo;fake&rdquo; version get disappointed anyway.</p>
<p>Isn&rsquo;t &ldquo;Cashew spread with herbs and spices&rdquo; more appealing? Need to market it? How about &ldquo;Cashew spread with a kick&rdquo; or something similar? It would also skip the chemicals they add to make these taste, look, and smell like the real thing. I think the &ldquo;fake milk&rdquo; industry is catching on, though slowly.</p>
